  "sourceInterpretation": "Official image reports ESP-IDFv6.1-dirty,exact private source revision unknown. Public clock LL/register headers fixed to fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643. esp_perip_clk_init selects modem LP source then calls periph_ll_clk_gate_set_default to disable unused modules; actual next ETM access matches this sequence. No physical-die calibration or network evidence.",
  "semantics": {
    "singleOwner": "MODEM_LPCON has one owner in Analog. EN bit2 and digital-master reset bit2 operate the existing actual I2C sequencer; target BIAS/DIG/PERIF storage is unchanged. No duplicate clock state.",
    "lpClocks": "BLE timer/COEX/Wi-Fi power selects existing40MHzXTAL or nominal136kHzRC_SLOW,divider+1. Parent and per-channel EN gates required. FORCE_ON is configuration,not an EN substitute. PMU state maps retained only; no sleep transitions synthesized.",
    "uartClocks": "UART1/2/3 exact0x83 reset,XTAL fractional dividers,independent APB/core gate/reset requests; no UART1/2/3 FIFO/IRQ/pin emulation. UART0 core gate no longer erroneously depends on APB enable. Four sleep-pad requests reset1,configuration only.",
    "unsupported": [
      "Digital RC_FAST/external32K and ambiguous LP source combinations",
      "Unimplemented LPCON radio/coex/BLE/DCMEM reset targets and AON forcing",
      "RF calibration,MAC/network/peer behavior,physical clock edge timing and PMU sleep/wakeup",
      "Auxiliary UART data-plane",
      "ETM and remaining startup peripheral clock words; Plus board/display"
    ]
  },
